**Date:** Sunday, January 10, 2010

**Title:** Lesson Plan- (Pre K - K): Baptism of Jesus

**Objectives:** The children will be able to

- retell the story of Jesus’ baptism
- identify that Jesus was baptized by John the Baptist
- identify that God said that Jesus was His beloved Son
- discuss why we are baptized

**Review:** Prayer and questions from last week’s lesson.

**Vocabulary Words:**  
The activity below is free, however it can only to be used for classroom and personal use. It may not be published on any websites or other electronic media, or distributed in newsletters, bulletins, or any other form or sold for profit. Reproduction or retransmission of any materials, in whole or in part, in any manner, is not permitted. All graphics/images/clipart etc. used on these activities are not my own and are from various internet sources.

[Baptism Word Wall](https://1drv.ms/b/s!Ar6LKlEjjtdHz3Ps7LOiggUueboW) Word wall templates are large flash card printables that you can hang on the wall to aid children when they are learning or using new vocabulary words. (Explain each card to the children. Example: Baptism- What is happening in this picture? The priest is pouring water on the baby’s head. This is baptism. John the Baptist- Who is this? John the Baptist. What is he wearing? Camel hair. What is he eating? Locusts and honey. Dove- What is this? A dove. What does it represent? The Holy Spirit. Beloved Son- What does this say? This is my beloved Son, with whom I am well pleased. This is what God said when Jesus was baptized.)

**Plan:**

### Circle Time:

Read story: “The Baptism of Jesus” from your own story book. Then ask questions from below.

- Who baptized Jesus? (John the Baptist)  
- Where did Jesus go to be baptized? (The Jordan River)  
- What did John the Baptist wear? (Camel hair)  
- What did John the Baptist eat? (Locusts and honey)  
- What did John the Baptist call people? (Brood of vipers)  
- What did John the Baptist say people must do to show they have changed their hearts? (Share with the poor, be honest, etc.)  
- Why did John the Baptist think he should be baptized by Jesus? (He said that Jesus was greater than him.)  
- What happened when Jesus was baptized? (The heavens opened, the Spirit of God descended like a dove, and a voice from heaven said, “This is my beloved Son, with whom I am well pleased.”)  
- What did God call Jesus? (My beloved Son)  
- What did God say He was well pleased with? (Jesus)  

**Discussion Questions:**  

- Why do you think Jesus was baptized? (To show us how to live, to fulfill all righteousness, etc.)  
- What does baptism mean? (We are washed clean from sin, we become children of God, etc.)  
- Why do we get baptized? (To be saved, to become part of God’s family, etc.)  

### Songs and/or Finger Plays:

Introduce songs and/or finger plays: Who baptized Jesus?  

- [dltk-bible.com-](http://www.dltk-bible.com/guides/jesus-baptism-song.htm) Baptism of Jesus Song  
- [sundayschoolnetwork.com-](http://www.sundayschoolnetwork.com/lessons/baptism.html) Baptism of Jesus (song)  

**Baptism of Jesus Finger Play:**  
(Do actions as you say the poem.)  
Jesus came to the river (walk to the front)  
To be baptized by John. (cup hands around mouth and call)  
John said, “No, Lord, baptize me!” (shake head no)  
But Jesus said, “It must be done.” (nod head yes)  
So John baptized Jesus (pour water on head)  
And God said from above, (look up)  
“This is my beloved Son (hug self)  
In whom I am well pleased.” (smile and nod)  

